        },
        {
          "insert": "pr-indexer",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "runMeleeKernelPiAgent()",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", forces the kernel spawn\npath for non-dry runs, attaches a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "postmortem",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " spawn context, records the\nresulting Pi session in harness state, and writes raw model output back to the\nPython worker. The Python launcher forwards orchestrator state/run/project and\nkernel DB settings so subprocess postmortems share the same app session,\ncontainer lineage, trace rows, and read API visibility as the rest of the\nrepresentative server job flow."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-running-integration-reso-36": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-running-integration-reso-36",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Running Integration Resolver"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-apps-server-src-core-ag-37": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-apps-server-src-core-ag-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/agent-catalog/agents/running/integration-resolver/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "\ndefines the pre-PR worker-output integration conflict agent. Its stable runtime\nid is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration-resolver",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The prompt receives one integration conflict queue\nitem plus a queue summary: failed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "git apply",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " evidence, worker checkpoint ids,\nexplicit write sets, conflict paths, validation evidence, and conflict-group\nmetadata. It returns "
        },
        {
          "insert": "melee_integration_resolver_result_v1",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with worker-output\ndispositions, path-level conflict resolutions, edits, validation rows, remaining\nconflicts, carry-forward notes, and risks."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-the-runtime-job-integra-38": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-the-runtime-job-integra-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The runtime job "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration-resolve --item-file <path>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " lives under the\nrunning phase and spawns this agent with kernel kind "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker-integration",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The\nrunner still owns queue status updates, epoch acceptance, and full build/report\nvalidation; clean worker checkpoint applies do not need this agent."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-pr-fixer-qa-repair-and-39": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-pr-fixer-qa-repair-and-39",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "PR Fixer, QA Repair, And Reconcile"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-apps-server-src-core-ag-40": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-apps-server-src-core-ag-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/agent-catalog/agents/pr/fixer/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " defines the opened-PR\nfeedback fixer. Its stable runtime id is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr-fixer",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The fixer receives\nmaintainer comments, review-thread findings, PR reviewer findings, diff\ncontext, and validation evidence for one PR branch. It returns\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "melee_pr_fixer_result_v1",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": focused edits, validation rows, comment/finding\ndispositions, remaining items, manual-review notes, and risks. The runner owns\nremote PR state, including posting comments or marking threads resolved."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-apps-server-src-core-ag-41": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-apps-server-src-core-ag-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/agent-catalog/agents/pr/qa-repair/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " defines the bounded\nQA repair queue surface.\nIts stable runtime id remains "
        },
        {
          "insert": "qa-repair",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for compatibility with the existing\ncandidate-file repair lane. The fixer receives one repair item plus its\nauthorized_write_set, fixes only the listed deterministic findings inside that\nscope, and returns the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "melee_qa_repair_result_v1",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "\nJSON contract. The runner owns partial reverts and final status: unauthorized\npaths are reverted without discarding authorized repair work, a required path\noutside the authorization becomes blocked_needs_cross_file, and agent output\nmust parse against the schema before the server job reruns the QA scanner and a\nfile can become\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "clean_same_match",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "clean_lower_score",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-the-legacy-reconcile-pro-42": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-the-legacy-reconcile-pro-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The legacy reconcile prompt lives under\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/agent-catalog/agents/pr/reconcile/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and remains exported\nas the PR phase reconcile prompt. It supports the existing operator-triggered\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "reconcile",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " command while bundle-wide repair behavior stays separate from PR\ncomment fixing. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "ship-validate",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " consumes the latest "
        },
        {
          "insert": "regression-check",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "\nsummary; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sync-merge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " runs after upstream sync fallout. Both refuse to run\nwhile the run status is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "active",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-the-pr-fixer-and-qa-r-43": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-the-pr-fixer-and-qa-r-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr-fixer",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "qa-repair",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " roles have separate tool profiles, registry\nentries, prompt tests, and dashboard Agent prompt previews. Their context\npackets include global decomp standards, targeted examples, attached tool lists,\nand output schemas so preview rendering stays aligned with live context\nconstruction."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
